[{"id":"VRCE-4-15-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":1,"english":"While residing in the female apartment, Vāli heard the uproar of that high-souled Sugriva-his wrathful brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffbddd9bfc213accc24e6f9a7b99bac2a3a677ae02d3cc1d0d19bb7e5274bbdf","compact":"4dc70b9b9fa65a7abb78fcf6266f7b086345d5b2fd73988fedec1f0e132c7145","nasal":"bca86bd9f746c695253cf3a3bd0a1f5e7fa9c74b0b37af6a87624e26ec4bda3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":2,"english":"And hearing that mighty roar, shaking the whole world of creation, his pride was in no time, crushed and he attained to an excess of ire.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.873,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a1904306af3c50fb45cdc0d52428108dc63cf205dbcde18b109526e732c0a10","compact":"6e9d7ed3736fea61b7d4e6ebd9f3d62bd2399baa49c79a51c3b82dd4ef4ad8c6","nasal":"89b90cee5e88e8aacfe3d05fca781546fd62422bf762e5cec1006620f724841c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":3,"english":"Thereupon, Vāli, having a golden hue, greatly exercised with wrath, instantly lost the effulgence of his person like to the sun possessed by Rāhu.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.712,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af708e308fe8d67c5078c5d5864d21a06a46b068223d95e13373d377422759c7","compact":"d30c9ef0401e9730bc239910abcc22c28af0c64b0e2e90d74a8c771e130ba952","nasal":"5adff0c28df23baf98924e33f62590b4919bc95c2b7d3e01f8804acf731a4e73"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":4,"english":"And looking terrible by his teeth and having eyes resembling burning fire in consequence of ire he appeared like to a pond, having the lotuses thereof uprooted with their stalks and fibres.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34dce4d5c119a78abed89d43825b0a1b37e50dd96e19ba486769d75924ab35b8","compact":"1648a77940bec636863b0a7533e05fc80ab472ab13c5b3ffc0faa15518870ee0","nasal":"1648a77940bec636863b0a7533e05fc80ab472ab13c5b3ffc0faa15518870ee0"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":5,"english":"And hearing that unbearable sound, the 'monkey, issued out speedily, as if riving the earth with his foot marks.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f3e64d05ea0acfe1f1cb3b7cc602903bed9a9764f9d23cf423fe4bb98461157f","compact":"98ab66ca8156d40fd44013c5fc90e0b73f8b898268d5cbe9dfe48d71b93e0e5b","nasal":"5cd9a6ae49127436a771864d0cedc1dcd9a5560423ad22f1fb312412d2413b1c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":6,"english":"Embracing him warmly and showing her affection, Tara, afraid and mortified, addressed him with the following words, presaging his future welfare.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ff720428bafbf359755cb5516e6f64345fbeb5457ac1378ad683d0789465ba59","compact":"0a2ba19e732a1443100a8ee44746da8ead7038d04eacb6f09ca4af0607bf6b8a","nasal":"0eb5889a228f9b703c3cbb46d6db23d1f4954ced375b3dc88383e10b335fdd91"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":7,"english":"Do you renounce, O hero, this your ire, coming like the course of a river, like to one, leaving aside the garland, which he used in the night, after rising from bed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d79148af5399d7f949220d282e2c01d6a8f3078ef81d6231edc4644d609fd5b0","compact":"44aab1b2565eae87d6d3d7ef917621da274c1fefdd557bc94975300a8dd8f94b","nasal":"44aab1b2565eae87d6d3d7ef917621da274c1fefdd557bc94975300a8dd8f94b"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":8,"english":"O monkey chief, do you engage with him in conflict, tomorrow. O hero, your enemy is very insignificant and hence there will be no deterioration on your part. Your hastily issuing out does not please me; do you hear, why I do prevent you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.683,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1acc1a20ec73c1e0e78e6f4301d9f769559413cb4fb1cadebd75a04535c66cfa","compact":"b46dff38dbf0aa21069847f9e50a08309d22667766dcb6de11c573bdb2ec8173","nasal":"a22940d652a686172d071d2eccc0267695d729b8c4263c85d0f74ce3b784b081"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":9,"english":"Formerly this Sugrīva invited you angrily to battle and being defeated and wounded by you fled away.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"af48934b6a45b0e8f6e2e778cdf1ca2deebb0ad3353c34a0843c8b4b917418c7","compact":"eb294633121444de5ebe404292090d45b0e09f82ff87f20e4d80a3ed9104f5da","nasal":"eb294633121444de5ebe404292090d45b0e09f82ff87f20e4d80a3ed9104f5da"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":10,"english":"That one, who had been defeated and harassed by you formerly, is now calling you. Indeed it has excited my fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"815e67c3ee284d286693a97e550c81a8b4ccf85a29921c223902bdfa0242f9d6","compact":"c0967c170b883e727c1c06b060b28678e4c218433827e01b756c0ae3aa5ddf07","nasal":"75f0cdf0a8ce14419e9472e271480f68b0a2efc347048117d90e3eb385bb1033"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":11,"english":"His pride, his energy, and his terrible uproar do indicate that there is nothing insignificant (at the bottom).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eee5cea1987caccdf5c0bcffb74f90ddd2c58b895d556bc2f86c44abbc0fcea2","compact":"bbd3ee590cbbfa7f4ef1cd685d899ee488430e539b066720103ce32424cc0a2b","nasal":"c856391badecf41178c830923b2a62283969a879004dbddf777e4c55c94c9176"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-12","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":12,"english":"I do not think Sugrīva has come here without any to assist him. Forsooth he has taken shelter of some body, and securing which he has been setting up such a terrible uproar.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015012","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3720a97e83948b94de00f9f6e49dd2dffa6f02431947e221a3f586339397683d","compact":"8d1531bfff538cb0b529eae79665320bde4efdaaa76843feb06050e7588934df","nasal":"8d1531bfff538cb0b529eae79665320bde4efdaaa76843feb06050e7588934df"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-13","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":13,"english":"That monkey is clever by nature and gifted with intellect. And Sugrīva shall not desire friendship with any one without having a test of his prowess.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015013","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c69f8d8374d5c563cf73032c2d770564eca8a8df2474d17ba5d549cae1ebf7e6","compact":"606b20e78e47587580e0c259bd262cd71e8d30fb804b896f1d2d9a55e95108e2","nasal":"606b20e78e47587580e0c259bd262cd71e8d30fb804b896f1d2d9a55e95108e2"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-14","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":14,"english":"Hearken, O hero, I shall relate to you today, the auspicious words, I heard ere this, from the prince Angada.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.789,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015014","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c71a723159f9108e27826b452b5dee6dc233777397f1b585095e0b208599aae9","compact":"560e59914593d93addc34a1e7f38a8a326ade0de6438eada49178ea9cb80ec8c","nasal":"e1d4761f48fcaa55a7b657197021dfc492a3fad05b4fe5757aefc1bdeb449530"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-15","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":15,"english":"To accomplish Sugrīva's welfare, those two heroes, hard to repress, have come here. He is the main stay of your brother in the battle. Rāma has sprung up like to the fire of dissolution and is the repressor of enemy's prowess. He is the refuge of the saints and the prime shelter of the afflicted.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015015","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"055a3fa50802a1d72293488f967a29730e3ea36cfa438be620df005554e19b57","compact":"8770540482f70362a4f99304b68d9d46cd38202cc4df6c69fcfc68bf56b83bbf","nasal":"b652a210ca71b9338b454ebc77383ef4f39014a8b88cbc69cf2cdfaddc72e1de"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-16","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":16,"english":"To accomplish Sugrīva's welfare, those two heroes, hard to repress, have come here. He is the main stay of your brother in the battle. Rāma has sprung up like to the fire of dissolution and is the repressor of enemy's prowess. He is the refuge of the saints and the prime shelter of the afflicted. He is the protector of those grinded by their enemies and is the only possessor of fame. He is gifted with knowledge and intellect and ever abideth by his sire's commandments,","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.433,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-17","DUTT-4-15-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015016","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"91c90d04d29e1eb80c045dcb98c4cb6476f46d284e1b1ee054eda5c4631c94ea","compact":"f4bd54d36a1fc805d322ded86a594aecfc983ae648c73687ca31825f9c75f77a","nasal":"6dec717484c7b630dc135939b117ac6ed3907fcce7502967c392de76e21a0db6"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-17","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":17,"english":"Like to Himālaya, the king of mountains, containing diverse metals, he is the mine of various accomplishments. It does not behove you therefore to enter into conflict with that high-souled Răma, incomparable in prowess and hard to conquer in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.333,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015017","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1daa31d6445e702e7214e432051cdaf87a5d8e9fae606b3f0bfa482bf8200690","compact":"51c5af8810dc06c729efcebbdd916bae4c6d0ae0228ce8ac028f9c49e43bd775","nasal":"6930d70c611c7d2277746f1554e2ad36ca9ac03c9ee000b4183a65fe76495cb5"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-18","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":18,"english":"Like to Himālaya, the king of mountains, containing diverse metals, he is the mine of various accomplishments. It does not behove you therefore to enter into conflict with that high-souled Răma, incomparable in prowess and hard to conquer in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.704,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015018","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"08a622725d9a02372a66ceed664330ad962bf720e6bd2e4bdba4ddd63f5fa21a","compact":"5f0c33b4f0fc97e3a42ef7359680a9a2aa5e93f6fb209a395c97b7a14cd436c9","nasal":"5f0c33b4f0fc97e3a42ef7359680a9a2aa5e93f6fb209a395c97b7a14cd436c9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-19","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":19,"english":"Hearken, O hero, I desire to speak something more-I do not wish to excite your wrath. Do you instantly confer upon Sugrīva, the dignity of heir apparent (to your throne). O hero, O king, do not quarrel with your younger brother.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.89,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015019","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b80b174db57b8a70ba941544f87df6d0beb18c1c8c95c3fe165cbd058f07c78b","compact":"4dd3b618525e294e020c9de47c63cc93a7de47d997b67876b1541167e0fff16c","nasal":"a0120c7dae731a021972fce9bec8f7ace972afea1dc5dd5cf76b03ba9752ca79"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-20","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":20,"english":"Hearken, O hero, I desire to speak something more-I do not wish to excite your wrath. Do you instantly confer upon Sugrīva, the dignity of heir apparent (to your throne). O hero, O king, do not quarrel with your younger brother.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.905,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015020","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c929da6ea8eef47a9eda9989855e8306b7a7975d152ebd4ae5373ebfaf54ebf0","compact":"73ac5eb8de149a44e559851a04767bf00a66b50e5b3a35d039a248e0a70c3b18","nasal":"73ac5eb8de149a44e559851a04767bf00a66b50e5b3a35d039a248e0a70c3b18"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-21","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":21,"english":"I do consider it your welfare to contract friendship with Rāma and regain Sugrīva's affections, renouncing all your inimical feelings.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015021","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5418dd40032c0eebc292eb94b3107e25841aa16c21b4fa088f5cc5ab6e56598","compact":"5ead0776dbd72b7599f190d18344a033954d546f1c7e2288a93a3dc0b85896c8","nasal":"5ead0776dbd72b7599f190d18344a033954d546f1c7e2288a93a3dc0b85896c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-22","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":22,"english":"This your younger brother, even when remaining at a distance, should always be maintained by you. Whether by you, or at a distance, he is always your best friend—I do not find his equal on earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015022","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e914a355e07327c60c72d9ba0b43aff61912a8a29b0bb5c4d9107878c6c4c823","compact":"e835e8fb2d8e9970c7ae96292602b07288949c1ce58ce7ca9994b5e6e29e5bac","nasal":"88665cc584f0a668e7a307679ad67359a09907605d94f5cc648d7fffe38c180e"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-15-23","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":15,"verse":23,"english":"If you does wish to go by my desire, if you does regard me as your well-wisher, do you perform what I do request you for your welfare. Be pleased and hear my beneficial words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.838,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-15-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4015023","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b2a7536cf23d49f5d0cce6625c098dad501b43b2e57bc3895b1545be0b881993","compact":"2d8eb50536fd949f769fd99e21f79a3d346b8725b900bc69a32d4e3bda3204cd","nasal":"2d8eb50536fd949f769fd99e21f79a3d346b8725b900bc69a32d4e3bda3204cd"}}]
